"Left to NumPy" counts calls that reached a hook and did not meet a kernel's
conditions: another element type, a strided array, an argument the kernel does
not implement. It is counted per NumPy call and shown on its first row.
Both columns count calls as written: np.argmax(m, axis=1) is one call, however
many rows NumPy splits it into. On the bn.* rows, calls to bottleneck's
functions, "Left to NumPy" counts calls left to bottleneck.
{% set uncounted = report.kernels | selectattr("installed") | selectattr("uncounted") | list %}
{% if uncounted %}
It is not counted for {% for kernel in uncounted %}{{ kernel.numpy_call }}{{ " and " if loop.revindex == 2 else (", " if not loop.last else "") }}{% endfor %}, since every add and
subtract of float64 arrays passes their hook.
{% endif %}
